**calibration.hpp defines validated, FOV-aware aim calibration for gamepad controllers.**

## Symbols

- `fov_scale(degrees fov, degrees reference_fov) noexcept -> float` scales turn rate by half-FOV tangent ratio; returns `1` at `reference_fov`.
- `aim_settings` stores authored `aim_profile hip`, `aim_profile ads`, `turn_integrator::limits accel`, optional `vector<knot> graph_knots`, and `bool graph_monotonic {true}`.
- `aim_calibration::make(const aim_settings&, string& why) -> optional<aim_calibration>` validates deadzones, curves, and constructed `aim_graph`, rejecting invalid configurations with a precise reason.
- `aim_calibration::processor_config() const noexcept -> aim_processor::config` returns processor settings referencing the owned graph.

## Invariants & Integration

`aim_calibration` owns `optional<aim_graph> graph_`; its lifetime must exceed processors created from `processor_config()`. `graph_monotonic` requires non-decreasing graph outputs. `types.hpp`, `utility.hpp`, `aim/types.hpp`, `aim/graph.hpp`, and `aim/assist.hpp` supply profiles, containers, graph construction, and processor configuration.